      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PAW ERIS (1) was prominent early from the tricky draw and did a fair job to be beaten a long neck into second (23.10) at Geelong in a Bottom Up - Grade 6 over 400m. Leading chance again. SNAPPER HEAD (4) broke from a low draw and filled a minor placing last start, beaten only half a length (23.11) behind Slay at Geelong. Will give a great sight again. ASTON MAJOR (8) doesn't have the best strike-rate. Better run when finding the frame last time though, finishing third (24.03) at Warragul. Hard to beat again. TIGER MOTH (6) is likely to have admirers.",
